    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Is it secure?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes. Connections are end to end encrypted and you are talking to your own
    machine. The pairing key never leaves your phone. The <a href="/#security"
      >security overview</a
    > covers the details.
  </p>

  <h2>Bottom line</h2>
  <p>
    If you only want to keep a Codex thread moving, the official mobile flow is
    fine. If you want to actually drive Codex, with a real mobile UI for slash
    commands, @ mentions, permissions, and models, plus a real terminal, your
    files, and Git behind it, Shellular runs Codex on your phone with nothing
    held back.
  </p>
